Version control remains crucial for developers, even when working solo on a project due to several reasons:

1. **Backup** - It serves as an automatic backup system that protects your work from accidental loss or corruption of files during the development process. Without version control, you risk losing significant progress if something goes wrong with local backups (e.g., hardware failure).
2. **Tracking Changes** - Even in solitary projects, understanding how changes evolve over time can be beneficial. You might realize patterns about what works well versus poorly implemented features based solely on personal experience without external feedback loops often provided by team environments. This self-awareness could lead to better coding practices moving forward. 
3. **Code Reviews & Learning Opportunities** - Although not mandatory like they are within teams, reviewing one's own past versions allows identifying mistakes made earlier which may have been missed initially but later discovered upon revisiting older commits after some delay—a valuable learning opportunity! Additionally, sharing these reviews publicly helps others learn too; hence fostering knowledge exchange among peers who aren’t necessarily part of any formal organization yet contribute significantly towards improving software quality across various domains collectively through their insights shared via platforms such as GitHub/GitLab etc..
4. **Collaboration Potential** - If at any point there arises interest in collaborating with other individuals interested in similar topics related to yours then having all necessary information organized neatly under source management tools becomes extremely helpful since starting collaboration requires accessibility into existing repositories containing relevant data points needed beforehand rather than spending considerable amount of effort trying figure out where things were kept previously leading delays especially considering most people tend forget easily unless reminded repeatedly until eventually giving up entirely resulting lost opportunities otherwise available had proper documentation existed right away instead relying memory laden processes only possible few times per day maximum usually depending heavily subjective recall abilities varying widely between different persons involved thus making overall productivity suffer greatly whenever lack documented history exists causing much frustration amongst participants alike regardless whether intentionally decided against using said systems originally either consci0ntiously ignorantly unaware its existence altogether never bother exploring further despite knowing full potential benefits offered thereby missing chances worth pursuing wholeheartedly should circumstances change unexpectedly requiring cooperation beyond initial scope envisioned ahead accordingly planning required preparations ensuring smooth transition seamlessly proceeding onto next phase successfully completing task assigned ultimately achieving desired outcome efficiently effectively utilizing resources optimally maximized output produced yielding superior results compared alternative methods employed less frequently adopted ones typically encountered throughout industry standard practice routinely followed presently observed globally today universally accepted normatively practiced regularly applied consistently worldwide recognized commonly